try</category><description>DeSpir Logistics, a C.H. Robinson company focused on high-value freight, has earned TAPA AMERICAS FBSR 2025 Tier 1 certification. The company describes DeSpir as among the first third-party logistics providers in North America to reach that top level for freight brokerage. TAPA, the Transported Asset Protection Association, sets cargo security and theft-prevention standards, and its Freight Broker Security Requirements certification is meant to reduce theft, fraud and loss on high-risk freight. According to the release, the certification covers DeSpir&#x27;s shipment planning, monitoring, chain-of-custody controls and incident response. C.H. Robinson acquired DeSpir on June 22, 2026, and said the deal expanded its network of vetted, security-focused contract carriers. The article also cites Verisk CargoNet figures showing industrywide theft losses of nearly $725 million in 2025.</description></item><item><title>AfA urges Congress to pass cargo theft bill</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/afa-urges-congress-to-pass-cargo-theft-bill-7dc42ef19b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/afa-urges-congress-to-pass-cargo-theft-bill-7dc42ef19b/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:00:10 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>STAT Times</description></item><item><title>DAT truckload freight trends from DAT One and DAT iQ</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/dat-truckload-freight-trends-from-dat-one-and-dat-iq-0eccb70e84/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/dat-truckload-freight-trends-from-dat-one-and-dat-iq-0eccb70e84/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:01:54 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>www.bluebookservices.com</description></item></channel></rss>